[c_029] C - Control Flow - Iteration (for & while)
Iteration Statements (for loops with C99/C11 loop variable declarations, while, do-while):
Example
Sumber: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-language/for-statement-c
## Example
This example illustrates the **`for`** statement:
Contoh Kode / Perintah CLI:
// c_for.c
int main()
{
   char* line = "H e  \tl\tlo World\0";
   int space = 0;
   int tab = 0;
   int i;
   int max = strlen(line);
   for (i = 0; i < max; i++ )
   {
      if ( line[i] == ' ' )
      {
          space++;
      }
      if ( line[i] == '\t' )
      {
          tab++;
      }
   }
   printf("Number of spaces: %i\n", space);
   printf("Number of tabs: %i\n", tab);
   return 0;
}

[c_033] C - Modern Features - C11/C17/C23 Generic Selection
Generic Selection (_Generic keyword for type-directed macro dispatch and
polymorphism): Example
Sumber: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-language/generic-selection
## Example
One way to use **`_Generic`** is in a macro. The \ header file uses **`_Generic`** to call the right math function
depending on the type of argument. For example, the macro for `cos` maps a call with a float to `cosf`, while mapping a
call with a complex double to `ccos`.
The following example shows how to write a macro that identifies the type of the argument you pass to it. It produces
`"unknown"` if no entry in the *`assoc-list`* matches the controlling expression:
Contoh Kode / Perintah CLI:
// Compile with /std:c11
#include <stdio.h>
/* Get a type name string for the argument x */
#define TYPE_NAME(X) _Generic((X), \
      int: "int", \
      char: "char", \
      double: "double", \
      default: "unknown")
int main()
{
    printf("Type name: %s\n", TYPE_NAME(42.42));
    // The following would result in a compile error because 
    // 42.4 is a double, doesn't match anything in the list, 
    // and there is no default.
    // _Generic(42.4, int: "integer", char: "character"));
}
