Sumber: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/Expression_statement
An **expression statement** is an expression used in a place where a statement is expected. The expression is evaluated and
its result is discarded  --  therefore, it makes sense only for expressions that have side effects, such as executing a function or
updating a variable.
## Syntax
js-nolint
expression;
- `expression`
