An **input boundary assertion** checks if the current position in the string is an input boundary. An input boundary is the start
or end of the string; or, if the `m` flag is set, the start or end of a line.
> [!NOTE]
> To match the start and end of the entire string in `m` mode, use the [buffer boundary
assertions](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Regular_expressions/Buffer_boundary_assertion) `\A`, `\z`, and `\Z`.
## Syntax
