## Syntax
js-nolint
-x
## Description
The `-` operator is overloaded for two types of operands: number and
[BigInt](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/BigInt). It first [coerces the operand to a numeric
value](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Data_structures#numeric_coercion) and tests the type of it. It performs BigInt
negation if the operand becomes a BigInt; otherwise, it performs number negation.
## Examples
### Negating numbers
const x = 3;
const y = -x;
// y is -3; x is 3
### Negating non-numbers
The unary negation operator can convert a non-number into a number.
const x = "4";
const y = -x;
// y is -4
BigInts can be negated using the unary negation operator.
const x = 4n;
const y = -x;
// y is -4n
