Sumber: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/RangeError
The **`RangeError`** object indicates an error when a value is not in the set or range of allowed values.
## Description
A `RangeError` is thrown when trying to pass a value as an argument to a function that does not allow a range that includes
the value.
This can be encountered when:
- passing a value that is not one of the allowed string values to String.prototype.normalize(), or
- when attempting to create an array of an illegal length with the Array constructor, or
- when passing bad values to the numeric methods Number.prototype.toExponential(), Number.prototype.toFixed() or
Number.prototype.toPrecision().
`RangeError` is a serializable object, so it can be cloned with {{DOMxRef("Window.structuredClone", "structuredClone()")}} or
copied between [Workers](/en-US/docs/Web/API/Worker) using {{domxref("Worker/postMessage()", "postMessage()")}}.
`RangeError` is a subclass of Error.
