The **`Promise.all()`** static method takes an iterable of promises as input and returns a single Promise. This returned
promise fulfills when all of the input's promises fulfill (including when an empty iterable is passed), with an array of the
fulfillment values. It rejects when any of the input's promises rejects, with this first rejection reason.
