The **`Error.stackTraceLimit`** static data property indicates the maximum number of stack frames captured by the stack trace
of an error. It can be set by user code to change the engine's behavior.
Generally, _reading_ this property is not very useful, but you can _set_ it to a new value. Setting it to a larger value can be
