arguments[1]; // second argument
arguments[2]; // third argument
The `arguments` object is useful for functions called with more arguments than they are formally declared to accept, called
[_variadic functions_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variadic_function), such as Math.min(). This example function accepts any
number of string arguments and returns the longest one:
