of parameters they are passed. That is, assigning new values to parameters in the body of the function never affects the
`arguments` object, nor will assigning new values to the `arguments` indices affect the value of parameters, even when the
function only has simple parameters.
> [!NOTE]
> You cannot write a `"use strict";` directive in the body of a function definition that accepts rest, default, or destructured
