Getters give you a way to _define_ a property of an object, but they do not _calculate_ the property's value until it is accessed.
A getter defers the cost of calculating the value until the value is needed. If it is never needed, you never pay the cost.
An additional optimization technique to lazify or delay the calculation of a property value and cache it for later access are
