When returning an immediately-resolved or immediately-rejected Promise, you do not need to create a `new Promise(...)` and
act on it. Instead, use the [`Promise.resolve()`](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/resolve) or
[`Promise.reject()`](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/reject) [static
methods](<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Method_(computer_programming)#Static_methods>).
This is not legal (the [`Promise` constructor](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/Promise) is not
being called correctly) and will throw a `TypeError: this is not a constructor` exception:
