Public instance fields are added to the instance either at construction time in the base class (before the constructor body runs),
or just after `super()` returns in a subclass. Fields without initializers are initialized to `undefined`. Like properties, field names
may be computed.
const PREFIX = "prefix";
class ClassWithField {
  field;
  fieldWithInitializer = "instance field";
  [`${PREFIX}Field`] = "prefixed field";
}
