construction, and [`super`](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/super) refers to the `prototype` property of the
base class, which contains the base class's instance methods, but not its instance fields.
class Base {
  baseField = "base field";
  anotherBaseField = this.baseField;
  baseMethod() {
    return "base method output";
  }
