field initializers, in the order they are declared.
Any static initialization of a super class is performed first, before that of its sub classes.
The scope of the variables declared inside the static block is local to the block. This includes `var`, `function`, `const`, and `let`
declarations. `var` declarations will not be hoisted out of the static block.
