When using sealed classes with `when` expressions, you can also add guard conditions to include additional checks in
a single branch.
For more information, see Guard conditions in when expressions.
> In multiplatform projects, if you have a sealed class with a `when` expression as an
> expected declaration in your common code, you still need an `else` branch.
> This is because subclasses of `actual` platform implementations may extend sealed classes that
> aren't known in the common code.
